From 429ad6ff9e5d27cdf18bc5a36a6159ede2d95d67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lavenly <135024283+lavenly@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 03:19:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] telephony: fix NPE in updateServiceStateArfcnRsrpBoost

When a device loses data registration or falls back to a network
state where the CellIdentity type is NONE, the framework correctly
parses the cell identity as null.

However, updateServiceStateArfcnRsrpBoost() unconditionally
calls cellIdentity.getType() without checking for null. On devices
with older RILs (e.g., Samsung Exynos) that regularly return
empty cell identities when disconnected, this results in a fatal
NullPointerException in ServiceStateTracker.

Because this exception crashes the state poll loop, the telephony
state machine infinitely retries, causing the telephony-radio
wakelock to be held indefinitely and severely draining the battery.

This patch adds a simple null safety check to ensure we safely
return early if the cell identity is null, porting forward the
safety check that existed in Android 10's getLteEarfcn().

Generated with Antigravity (https://antigravity.google) using Gemini 3.1 Pro (High)

Change-Id: I15e0b60d188221b62b86cacdd44005872345e39a
